config MGBA
	bool "mGBA Game Boy Advance emulator core"
	depends on RISCV
	select FILE_SYSTEM
	help
	  Build the Game Boy Advance core of mGBA (the git submodule mgba/)
	  as a library without threading, debugger, scripting or image
	  codecs. The mGBA software renderer draws RGB565 frames; the
	  built-in BIOS replacement is used, no BIOS file is needed.

if MGBA

config MGBA_RVV
	bool "Vector versions of hot loops (needs the V extension)"
	default y if SUN252I_F101_RVV
	help
	  The emulator library is built with the V extension; copies and
	  fills, and the background renderer use the vector unit.

config MGBA_ROM_DEMAND_PAGED
	bool "Map the ROM as a demand paged file"
	depends on DEMAND_PAGING && BACKING_STORE_FS
	help
	  Instead of reading the whole ROM into memory it is mapped from
	  the file system and the pages come in when the emulation touches
	  them, so a 16 MiB ROM needs only the page frames that are left.
	  Needs the MMU of the kernel and enough page frames: the memory
	  that is not malloc arena or image.

config MGBA_MAX_ROM_SIZE_MB
	int "Largest ROM that is read into memory (MiB)"
	default 32
	range 1 32
	help
	  With MGBA_ROM_DEMAND_PAGED the limit is the address space of the
	  cartridge, 32 MiB.

endif # MGBA
